---
import LegalPage from "../components/legal/legal-page.astro";

const toc = [
  { id: "overview", title: "Overview & Data Controller" },
  { id: "data-we-collect", title: "Information We Collect" },
  { id: "how-we-use-data", title: "How We Use Your Data" },
  { id: "data-sharing", title: "Data Sharing & Third Parties" },
  { id: "media-recordings", title: "Livestreaming & Media Recordings" },
  { id: "security-retention", title: "Data Security & Retention" },
  { id: "your-rights", title: "Your Rights (UU PDP)" },
  { id: "policy-changes", title: "Changes to This Policy" },
  { id: "contact", title: "Privacy Contact & Inquiries" },
];
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  subtitle="How PERKODI collects, uses, protects, and handles personal data for IDSW 2026 in compliance with Indonesian Data Protection Law (UU PDP)."
  toc={toc}
  currentPath="/privacy-policy">
  <div class="rounded-xl border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50/60 p-5 text-sm text-blue-950">
    <p class="font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-1">Our Privacy Commitment</p>
    <p class="text-blue-900/90 leading-relaxed">
      PERKODI respects your personal privacy. We collect and process personal data exclusively for organizing,
      administering, and delivering IDSW 2026. We never sell personal data to advertisers or third-party brokers.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 1: Overview -->
  <section id="overview" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      1. Overview & Data Controller
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Perkumpulan Pengrajin Kode Indonesia (PERKODI)</strong> (“PERKODI”, “we”, “us”,
      or “our”) acts as the data controller for personal data collected in connection with <strong
        >Indonesia Software Developer Weekend 2026 (IDSW 2026)</strong
      > and its official website (<a href="https://idsw.dev" class="text-primary underline">idsw.dev</a>).
    </p>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      Our data processing practices are designed to comply with <strong
        >Law of the Republic of Indonesia No. 27 of 2022 on Personal Data Protection (Undang-Undang Perlindungan Data
        Pribadi / UU PDP)</strong
      > and applicable electronic transaction regulations.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2: Information We Collect -->
  <section id="data-we-collect" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      2. Information We Collect
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      Depending on how you engage with IDSW 2026 (as an attendee, speaker, volunteer, or partner), we may collect:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
      <li>
        <strong>Identification & Contact Data:</strong> Full name, professional email address, telephone/WhatsApp number,
        job title, company or organization, and city of residence.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Ticketing & Attendance Records:</strong> Ticket tier, order identifier, check-in status at Usmar Ismail Hall,
        and badge issuance metadata. Financial payment details (such as credit card numbers or bank accounts) are processed
        directly by our secure ticketing partner (TipTip) and are never stored on IDSW servers.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Speaker & CFP Submissions:</strong> Speaker biography, headshot photo, presentation titles, abstracts, slides,
        source code repositories, and technical topic preferences.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Communications & Feedback:</strong> Inquiries sent to our email desk, survey responses, and feedback submissions.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Technical & Analytics Data:</strong> IP address, device type, browser information, and aggregated website
        interaction metrics collected via privacy-friendly analytics tools.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 3: How We Use Your Data -->
  <section id="how-we-use-data" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      3. How We Use Your Data
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      We process your personal information strictly for legitimate conference management purposes:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
      <li>Administering ticket purchases, issuing conference passes, and verifying on-site check-in credentials.</li>
      <li>
        Delivering vital operational announcements, schedule updates, venue logistical guides, and security alerts.
      </li>
      <li>Reviewing, selecting, and scheduling Call for Proposals (CFP) presentations.</li>
      <li>
        Publishing speaker names, profile bios, and talk details on the official conference schedule and promotion
        channels.
      </li>
      <li>Responding to support requests, Code of Conduct incident reports, and general inquiries.</li>
      <li>
        Maintaining internal financial accounting, tax compliance, and auditing records as mandated by Indonesian law.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 4: Data Sharing & Third Parties -->
  <section id="data-sharing" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      4. Data Sharing & Third Parties
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      We do not rent, trade, or sell your personal data. We only share data with trusted third parties under binding
      confidentiality and data protection agreements:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
      <li>
        <strong>Ticketing Partner (TipTip):</strong> To process ticket purchases, manage inventory, and validate access badges.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Livestreaming & Media Infrastructure (YouTube, Vimeo, Cloudflare):</strong> To deliver real-time session streaming
        and on-demand digital archives for online participants.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Venue & Security Management:</strong> In-person attendee headcounts and emergency security records shared
        with Usmar Ismail Hall management where legally or logistically required.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legal & Regulatory Authorities:</strong> When required by Indonesian statutory law, court summons, or in response
        to an active law enforcement investigation.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sponsors & Community Partners:</strong> Aggregated, anonymized demographic statistics (e.g. total attendee
        count, attendee role breakdowns) may be shared with sponsors. Personally identifiable contact information is <em
          >never</em
        > shared without your explicit opt-in consent.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 5: Livestreaming & Media Recordings -->
  <section id="media-recordings" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      5. Livestreaming & Media Recordings
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      As a large-scale community conference, IDSW 2026 sessions are recorded, photographed, and broadcast:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
      <li>
        Auditorium presentations, panel discussions, and Q&A sessions may be live-streamed publicly and archived on
        official video channels for community education.
      </li>
      <li>Crowd and ambient event photography may capture attendee likenesses in public conference areas.</li>
      <li>
        If you wish to opt out of being featured in close-up media or public video footage, please notify the organizing
        committee in advance via <a href="mailto:idsw.ticketing@perkodi.org" class="text-primary underline"
          >idsw.ticketing@perkodi.org</a
        > so we can arrange accommodations where feasible.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 6: Data Security & Retention -->
  <section id="security-retention" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      6. Data Security & Retention
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      We enforce administrative, organizational, and technical safeguards to protect your personal data against
      unauthorized access, destruction, loss, alteration, or unlawful disclosure:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-700">
      <li>
        Access to participant data is restricted solely to authorized members of the PERKODI organizing desk who need it
        for event operations.
      </li>
      <li>
        All data transmissions between your browser and our services are encrypted using Transport Layer Security
        (TLS/HTTPS).
      </li>
      <li>
        Personal data is retained only as long as necessary to fulfill conference management and legal compliance
        duties, after which it is deleted or permanently anonymized.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 7: Your Rights -->
  <section id="your-rights" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      7. Your Rights Under Indonesian Law (UU PDP)
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      Under the Indonesian Personal Data Protection Act (UU No. 27/2022), you hold specific rights regarding your
      personal information:
    </p>
    <div class="grid gap-3 pt-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 p-3.5 text-xs text-neutral-700">
        <span class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 block mb-1">Right to Access & Information</span>
        Obtain clarity on how your personal data is collected, used, and processed.
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 p-3.5 text-xs text-neutral-700">
        <span class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 block mb-1">Right to Rectification</span>
        Request corrections or updates to inaccurate, outdated, or incomplete data.
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 p-3.5 text-xs text-neutral-700">
        <span class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 block mb-1">Right to Erasure</span>
        Request deletion or destruction of your personal data when no longer needed.
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 p-3.5 text-xs text-neutral-700">
        <span class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 block mb-1">Right to Withdraw Consent</span>
        Withdraw prior consent for non-essential communications or marketing updates.
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-neutral-500 pt-1">
      To exercise any of these rights, please email our data desk at <a
        href="mailto:idsw.ticketing@perkodi.org"
        class="text-primary underline">idsw.ticketing@perkodi.org</a
      >. We will review and respond to valid requests within statutory deadlines.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 8: Policy Changes -->
  <section id="policy-changes" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      8. Changes to This Policy
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      We may update this Privacy Policy periodically to reflect technological adjustments, new event features, or
      regulatory amendments in Indonesian privacy laws.
    </p>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      The most up-to-date policy will always be published on <a
        href="https://idsw.dev/privacy-policy"
        class="text-primary underline">idsw.dev/privacy-policy</a
      > with the updated effective date.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 9: Contact -->
  <section id="contact" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-3">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 border-b border-neutral-100 pb-2">
      9. Privacy Contact & Inquiries
    </h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      If you have questions, privacy concerns, or wish to exercise your statutory rights as a data subject, please
      contact:
    </p>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 p-5 text-sm text-neutral-700">
      <p class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">PERKUMPULAN PENGRAJIN KODE INDONESIA (PERKODI)</p>
      <p class="mt-1">Data Protection & Privacy Desk — IDSW 2026</p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Email: <a href="mailto:idsw.ticketing@perkodi.org" class="text-primary font-semibold underline"
          >idsw.ticketing@perkodi.org</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
